# L §8.2: "Every result lists, under it, the things it rests on that aren't plain sourced facts; a hole lists them
# like a value."  An assumed row read beside a hole.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
input g: int
input h: int

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  g = 1 assumed "a guess"
  h = ?"unknown"

ask q1: g + h
=== expect
q1: ?"unknown" (h)
  assumed: a guess (g)
  cut 2026-12-31
